# GitFactory local env — copy to `.env` and fill in for local testing:  cp .env.example .env
#
# ⚠ SECURITY (CLAUDE.md golden rule #7): this is a STATIC frontend. Vite inlines every
# VITE_* variable into the client bundle at build time. So the secret vars below are
# DEV-ONLY: the app reads them only under `import.meta.env.DEV`, and `vite.config.ts`
# HARD-FAILS `npm run build` if any secret var is set — a production bundle can never
# contain them. `.env` is gitignored; never commit real credentials.

# ── Build / dev (safe, not secret) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Base path for GitHub Pages (the deploy workflow sets this to /<repo-name>/).
# VITE_BASE=/gitorio/
# Reliable HMR inside Docker (set automatically by the docker-compose dev service).
# VITE_USE_POLLING=true

# ── DEV-ONLY local-testing credentials (⚠ never set these for a build) ───────
# A fine-grained PAT with Contents (RW) + Workflows (RW). When both VITE_GH_PAT and
# VITE_GH_REPO are set, `npm run dev` auto-connects on load so you don't re-paste the
# token every session. The token still only lands in sessionStorage at runtime.
# VITE_GH_PAT=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Repo to auto-connect to, as owner/name.
# VITE_GH_REPO=bamr87/lifehacker.dev

# Optional: pre-fills the "Connect power" key field in the Deploy modal for end-to-end
# testing. Entered in the UI otherwise; sealed-box encrypted, never stored.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
